pokeheartgold-saveptr.patch (tools/pokehg_gen.py applies the patches in name order): no host pointer in a map object's saved
movement data. MapObject_Save (map_object.c) copies each map object's 16-byte movement-data buffer (unkD8) into the save as it
is, and the load copies it back. Two movement types keep a pointer there:
 - UnkStruct_02069F48.unk_08, the MapObject a paired trainer follows (written by sub_020661CC, read by sub_020661F0);
 - UnkStruct_0206A0BC.unk_04, the OverworldAnimManager of a hidden object's effect (sub_02066420 / sub_0206642C).
On the DS each is a 4-byte address; on the host 8 bytes of host address, which moves with the binary (libntr's s_HW_MAIN_MEM): two
builds wrote different saves. Both are now u32 DS-style addresses (port_hgss.h PortHg_DsAddr / PortHg_HostAddr: 0x02000000 + the
offset in s_HW_MAIN_MEM), so the structs have the DS's size and the save the same bytes on every build. Nothing reads a saved value
back: the restore functions clear it (sub_02066370 sets unk_04 = 0; sub_02065CD0 sets unk_01 = 0 so unk_08 is set again before it
is read), so a save written before this change (a host pointer in those 8 bytes) loads as before.

